<<~ ahu #/head>>

! Pranala

One anchored pointer from this carrier outward.

The typed-edge law divides in three: ''composition'' rides the meta `tags` field (`has-stack`); ''relations that do something'' reify as wire entities (`wire`); ''pranala'' carries a named anchor pointing at a target, plus its sugar. The graph stays explicit; the types live in the things, never on the lines.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/ooda-ha>>

✶ find what the pointer really carries — composition, action, embed, or bare adjacency — before authoring.
⏿ orient on the ladder: worn → tags · doing → wire entity · embedding → aka/kahea · pointing → loulou or anchored pranala.
◇ decide the lightest lawful form; reach for pranala only when the anchor name earns its place.
▶ author one pointer per sigil; bind the target explicitly.
↺ verify no retired vocabulary rode in; fewer, lighter edges = the win condition.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/law>>

!! Pranala Law (Kānāwai)

# A pranala carries one ''anchored pointer'': `<<~ pranala #anchor from=? -> to=TARGET>>` — the `#anchor` names the pointer's office in this carrier; `?` resolves to the nearest enclosing socket or `#fragment-id`; `TARGET` names a `lar:` URI (optionally `#fragment`) or a repo file path.
# ''Retired-reserved (2026-06-12):'' the `role:` vocabulary (implements, owns, governed-by, and the rest of the feral taxonomy) and `family:` as an inline edge type. The corpus-wide burn converted them to tags, loulou, and (where relations //do// something) the wire plane. Retired terms stay reserved, never reused.
# ''One attributed form survives at rest:'' the code source-pointer — `<<~ pranala #anchor from=? -> to=packages/<path> family=code role=has>>` — until the parser's edge-field plane recuts; new attribute vocabulary MUST NOT mint.
# Sugar, unchanged: `<<~ loulou URI>>` (adjacency) · `<<~ aka URI>>` (shadow transclusion) · `<<~ kahea URI>>` (live transclusion).
# Anything heavier — direction, propagation, payload, lifecycle, arity — belongs to a ''wire entity'', never to this sigil.
# ''The carrier-grain wire form.'' An anchored body pranala MAY author a wire (`wire #authoring`): the sigil = the carrier-grain projection, the wire entity = the existence, the compiler (INGEST-era) = the shore between. Until the compiler lands, such sigils stand as declared-unresolved wires — lawful memory-palace placeholders, never errors.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/handoff-boundary>>

!! Handoff Boundary

`has-stack` governs composition (the tags field).
`wire` governs reified edges — the canvas and verse-messaging substrate (families, traversal, propagation, lifecycle template/instance/trace, the DAG rule — all moved there whole).
`pranala-families` holds the family taxonomy shelf the wire components grow from.
`papalohe` / `kukali` carry the messaging widgets; `verse-event-lattice` the engine-vended event law.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/edges>>

